<DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example17RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example17CsharpCode" Id="example17" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        Style and Class reach the root element, the Style and Class selectors reach a single item, and the
        Styles and Classes objects reach every part of the timeline separately: the item, the two contents,
        the two texts, the divider, the dot and the icon. The connecting line is painted by a pseudo-element
        of the divider, so its color is set through the --bit-tln-dvd-clr variable on the divider's style.
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Component's Style & Class:</div><br />
    <BitTimeline Style="max-width: max-content; color: dodgerblue;" Items="basicCustoms" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
    <br /><br />
    <BitTimeline Horizontal Class="custom-class" Items="basicCustoms" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
    <br /><br /><br /><br />
    <div>Item's Style & Class:</div><br />
    <BitTimeline Items="styleClassCustoms" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
    <br /><br /><br /><br />
    <div><b>Styles</b> & <b>Classes</b>:</div><br />
    <div class="example-content">
        <BitTimeline Items="iconCustoms" NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Styles="@(new() { Icon = "color: whitesmoke;",
                                           Dot = "background-color: lightseagreen; border-color: mediumseagreen;",
                                           PrimaryText = "color: lightseagreen; font-weight: bold;" })" />
        <BitTimeline Items="iconCustoms" NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                     Variant="BitVariant.Outline"
                     Classes="@(new() { Dot = "custom-dot",
                                            Icon = "custom-icon",
                                            Item = "custom-item-text",
                                            Divider = "custom-divider" })" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

